Three files in templates/ and the samples in testdata/ntc/ come from ntc-templates
(https://github.com/networktocode/ntc-templates, commit d86d09fa105ee2a432795022e7df04737c65dd28),
Copyright 2015 Jason Edelman and Network to Code, LLC, licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. The full license text is in testdata/ntc/LICENSE-ntc-templates.

Changes:
- templates/show_lldp_neighbors_detail.textfsm: from cisco_ios_show_lldp_neighbors_detail.textfsm.
  Only the values the neighbours recipe maps are kept (local interface, chassis ID, port ID,
  system name, management address); the description, capability, VLAN, MAC, power and LLDP-MED
  values are dropped and their lines skipped. Added the MGMT_ADDRESS_SUBTYPE value and the
  Addresses, AddressesV6 and AddressesDone states, so a block's management address is its first
  IPv4 address, else its first IPv6 one, stored with its type; upstream keeps the last IPv4 line.
- templates/show_interfaces.textfsm: from cisco_ios_show_interfaces.textfsm, renamed INTERFACE to
  PORT. Only port, states, MAC, description and MTU are kept; addresses, counters, rates, queues,
  encapsulation and timers are dropped. PROTOCOL_STATUS is the first word after "line protocol
  is", without the "(connected)" or ", Autostate Enabled" that follows. Added the LINK_SPEED value,
  the speed of a port that is up read from the duplex line ("1000Mb/s" gives 1000M).
- templates/show_interfaces_switchport.textfsm: rewritten from cisco_ios_show_interfaces_switchport
  .textfsm, keeping its block structure (one record per "Name:" block). Only interface, mode,
  access VLAN and port-channel are kept; the mode is the operational one, or the administrative one
  when the port is down; the access VLAN is read on access ports only; a port-channel member gives
  its channel and nothing else; a routed port gives no row.
- testdata/ntc/: raw samples only, renamed without the cisco_ios_ prefix:
  show_lldp_neighbors_detail.raw, show_lldp_neighbors_detail2.raw and
  show_lldp_neighbors_detail3.raw from tests/cisco_ios/show_lldp_neighbors_detail/
  cisco_ios_show_lldp_neighbors_detail1.raw to 3; show_interfaces.raw and show_interfaces2.raw
  from tests/cisco_ios/show_interfaces/cisco_ios_show_interfaces6.raw and
  cisco_ios_show_interfaces_01.raw; show_interfaces_switchport.raw and
  show_interfaces_switchport2.raw from tests/cisco_ios/show_interfaces_switchport/
  cisco_ios_show_interfaces_switchport_app_interfaces.raw and
  cisco_ios_show_interfaces_switchport3.raw. Their .yml files are not copied, since the templates
  above keep other values under other names: each .yml next to a sample was written for this pack
  from what its template extracts, and checked against the upstream .yml on every field both keep
  (ports, chassis ID, names, addresses, states, MAC, MTU, mode, access VLAN).

templates/show_vlan_brief.textfsm and templates/show_interfaces_trunk.textfsm are not from
ntc-templates.
